/**
  @page examples-pdes-dg-poisson Solving diffusion with discontinuous Galerkin
  @brief Assemble and validate a symmetric interior-penalty method on triangles.

  @tableofcontents
  @m_footernavigation

  @section examples-dg-setting Problem and discrete space

  On @f$\Omega=(0,1)^2@f$, solve
  @f[
    -\Delta u=f\quad\text{in }\Omega,\qquad u=g\quad\text{on }\partial\Omega.
  @f]
  The discontinuous space is
  @f[
    V_h=\{v\in L^2(\Omega):v|_K\in\mathbb P_1(K)
      \text{ for every }K\in\mathcal T_h\}.
  @f]
  Each triangle owns three affine coefficients. Neighboring triangles have
  independent values at a shared geometric vertex. Thus a mesh with
  @f$N_K@f$ cells has @f$3N_K@f$ unknowns.

  This example assembles the cell and facet matrices explicitly using Rodin
  meshes, mapped quadrature and sparse algebra. The implementation is scoped
  to affine two-dimensional triangles. Making every local block visible
  connects the consistency and penalty terms to their actual matrix entries.

  @section examples-dg-fluxes Interior flux and penalty

  For each interior facet, order the cells as @f$K^+,K^-@f$ and choose
  @f$n_F@f$ outward from @f$K^+@f$. Define
  @f[
    [\![v]\!]=v^+-v^-,\qquad
    \{\nabla v\}=\tfrac12(\nabla v^++\nabla v^-).
  @f]
  With facet length @f$h_F@f$ and @f$\sigma_F=20/h_F@f$, the symmetric form is
  @f[
  \begin{aligned}
    a_h(u,v)={}&\sum_K\int_K\nabla u\cdot\nabla v\\
      &-\sum_{F\in\mathcal F_i}\int_F\{\nabla u\}\cdot n_F[\![v]\!]
       -\sum_{F\in\mathcal F_i}\int_F\{\nabla v\}\cdot n_F[\![u]\!]\\
      &+\sum_{F\in\mathcal F_i}\int_F\sigma_F[\![u]\!][\![v]\!]\\
      &-\int_{\partial\Omega}(\nabla u\cdot n)v
       -\int_{\partial\Omega}(\nabla v\cdot n)u
       +\int_{\partial\Omega}\sigma_Fuv.
  \end{aligned}
  @f]
  The right-hand side is
  @f[
    \ell_h(v)=\int_\Omega fv
       -\int_{\partial\Omega}(\nabla v\cdot n)g
       +\int_{\partial\Omega}\sigma_Fgv.
  @f]
  Boundary coefficients remain unknown. The boundary terms impose the data
  weakly. The penalty value is a fixed choice for the degree-one,
  shape-regular meshes studied here; other degrees or cell shapes require
  an appropriate penalty analysis.

  @section examples-dg-assembly Cell and facet matrices

  On the reference triangle, the basis is
  @f$(1-r-s,r,s)@f$. Its physical gradients are obtained with
  @f$DF_K^{-T}@f$. Index @f$3k+i@f$ identifies local basis function @f$i@f$
  in cell @f$k@f$.

  @snippet DG/Poisson.cpp dg-local-space
  @snippet DG/Poisson.cpp dg-cells

  An interior facet contributes a six-by-six block over both cells. A boundary
  facet contributes a three-by-three block and a load vector. The implementation
  uses the same normal and cell ordering in every jump and flux term.

  @snippet DG/Poisson.cpp dg-facets

  Degree-ten quadrature integrates the polynomial stiffness and penalty
  terms exactly on these affine cells. It also resolves the smooth prescribed
  source and error integrals used in the refinement study.

  @section examples-dg-solve Solve and check the algebra

  The assembled matrix is checked for relative symmetry. A sparse LDLT
  factorization checks positive pivots, solves the system and reports the
  relative algebraic residual. These checks concern each actual assembled
  system in the study.

  @snippet DG/Poisson.cpp dg-solve

  Stability and optimal error estimates for consistent interior-penalty
  methods are developed by Arnold, Brezzi, Cockburn and Marini
  @cite arnold2002unified.

  @section examples-dg-validation Patch test and refinement study

  The first case is @f$u=1+x+2y@f$, with zero source and nonzero Dirichlet
  data. It is exactly representable in the discontinuous affine space. The
  measured @f$L^2@f$ error is @f$5.10\times10^{-15}@f$ and the broken-gradient
  error is @f$3.05\times10^{-14}@f$.

  The second case uses
  @f[
    u=1+x+2y+\sin(\pi x)\sin(\pi y),\qquad
    f=2\pi^2\sin(\pi x)\sin(\pi y).
  @f]
  The program refines the mesh while retaining the degree, penalty convention,
  source, boundary data and quadrature order.

  | Intervals per axis | Unknowns | @f$\|u-u_h\|_{L^2}@f$ | @f$|u-u_h|_{H^1(\mathcal T_h)}@f$ |
  | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
  | 4 | 96 | @f$6.0663\times10^{-2}@f$ | @f$7.4403\times10^{-1}@f$ |
  | 8 | 384 | @f$1.7217\times10^{-2}@f$ | @f$3.8657\times10^{-1}@f$ |
  | 16 | 1,536 | @f$4.5076\times10^{-3}@f$ | @f$1.9561\times10^{-1}@f$ |
  | 32 | 6,144 | @f$1.1471\times10^{-3}@f$ | @f$9.8211\times10^{-2}@f$ |

  @image html DGConvergence.png "Measured errors and reference slopes for the SIPG refinement study."

  The final refinement gives observed orders approximately 1.97 and 0.99.
  The unweighted interior jump norm decreases from 0.02846 to 0.001506.
  The relative matrix-symmetry discrepancy stays below
  @f$2.3\times10^{-17}@f$ and the relative solution residual below
  @f$1.7\times10^{-15}@f$. Positive LDLT pivots are checked at every level.

  @section examples-dg-output Preserve separate traces in visualization

  @image html DGPoisson.png "Computed DG fields on coarse and fine meshes. Each cell retains its own exported vertex values."

  The XDMF output duplicates geometric vertices for each cell so ParaView
  retains the cell-local values. Open `DGCoarse.xdmf` or `DGPoisson.xdmf`,
  select **Apply**, then color by **u**. Keep the original cell-local
  representation when inspecting jumps.

  @section examples-dg-run Build and run

  Build `DGPoisson` and run it in a scratch directory. It executes the patch
  test and all four refinement levels serially, writes `DGConvergence.csv`
  and exports the coarse and finest smooth-case fields. It returns
  `EXIT_FAILURE` if factorization, patch accuracy, symmetry, residual,
  decreasing jumps or the required refinement ratios fail.

  @ref DG/Poisson.cpp "Complete source code" contains the assembly,
  numerical checks and visualization export.

  @section examples-dg-next Continue

  - @ref examples-interface-traces "Inspect two-sided values directly"
  - @ref guides-interfaces-dg "Facet vocabulary and assumptions"
  - @ref examples-pdes-poisson "Conforming diffusion formulation"

  @example DG/Poisson.cpp
  @m_footernavigation
*/
